Implementation of Merge Sort using the Divide-and-Conquer approach with analysis of time complexity.
# Experiment 01 – Merge Sort

## Aim
Implement Divide-and-Conquer algorithms for merge sort and calculate their time complexities.

## Algorithm / Procedure
1. Divide the array into two halves.
2. Recursively sort both halves.
3. Merge the sorted halves.
4. Continue until the complete array is sorted.

## Program
def merge_sort(a):
    if len(a) <= 1:
        return a

    mid = len(a) // 2
    left = merge_sort(a[:mid])
    right = merge_sort(a[mid:])

    return sorted(left + right)

a = [5, 2, 8, 1, 3]
print("Sorted:", merge_sort(a))

## Output
[Sorted: [1, 2, 3, 5, 8]]

## Time Complexity
O(n log n)

## Space Complexity
O(n)

## Result
The Merge Sort algorithm was successfully implemented using the Divide-and-Conquer approach.
